-- Delta migration (canonical spec SPEC-CANONICAL.md, adopted 2026-11-16; design D1 in
-- .kiro/specs/seeds-v2-delta/design.md). Generated by drizzle-kit from lib/db/schema.ts, then
-- hand-corrected:
--   * the table rebuilds copy ONLY the pre-existing columns (drizzle-kit 0.31 selects new
--     columns from the old table, which fails on populated databases);
--   * `PRAGMA foreign_keys=OFF/ON` (a no-op inside D1's migration transaction) is replaced by
--     `PRAGMA defer_foreign_keys = on`, and each rebuild is backup → DROP → CREATE (real name) →
--     re-INSERT → drop backup. Re-inserting the parent keys clears SQLite's deferred-FK counter;
--     the create-new + RENAME pattern does not (verified: it fails at COMMIT with child rows);
--   * the FTS triggers from 0001 are dropped first (DROP TABLE varieties would drop three of
--     them anyway) and recreated unchanged at the end. Variety ids (= FTS rowids) are copied
--     explicitly, so the FTS index stays valid;
--   * existing listings that share one product_url per seller (curated collection pages) get
--     variant_key = 'variety:<slug>' so the new UNIQUE (seller_id, product_url, variant_key)
--     holds; the importer applies the same rule;
--   * catalog_meta is seeded with catalog_seq = 0.
-- Rebuilt tables: listings, varieties, sellers, variety_aliases (new CHECK constraints / unique
-- key). Not enforced on purpose: the canonical CHECK (approved ⇒ terms_reviewed_at NOT NULL).
PRAGMA defer_foreign_keys = on;
